Neutron: font links reach a family that is present only as a Replacement.

Bridge 2026's Label menu drew its rating stars (U+2605) as empty boxes. Bridge's menus are plain Win32 text menus drawn
by win32u in the system menu font, and no font in the prefix's fallback chain had the star.
Windows 11 (starprobe, 2026-11-07): the menu font is Segoe UI, which has no star. GDI takes the star through the font
links: Segoe UI's SystemLink list (Tahoma, Meiryo UI, MS UI Gothic, ... Yu Gothic UI, Segoe UI Symbol) and Tahoma's list
(MS UI Gothic, PMingLiU, SimSun, Gulim, Yu Gothic UI, JhengHei UI, YaHei UI, Malgun Gothic, Segoe UI Symbol) both reach a
font that has it; the first is MS UI Gothic, and Segoe UI Symbol, last in both, has it too. DirectWrite maps the star to
Segoe UI Symbol. Wine's wine.inf carries Tahoma's list exactly as Windows has it, and win32u appends Tahoma's and Microsoft
Sans Serif's links to every font. But SystemLink entries are matched by FILE name, and a Neutron prefix has those families
only as Replacements (HKCU\Software\Wine\Fonts\Replacements), whose stand-ins' files never carry Microsoft's names, so
every link was dropped. A Replacement declares that the stand-in IS that family, so a link to a replaced family now
resolves to the stand-in's regular face when no face has the named file. Real fonts and links to installed files are
matched as before, in Windows' order.
Needs the CLI to give "Segoe UI Symbol" a stand-in that has its glyphs (CLI branch starfont: REG_MULTI_SZ "Noto Sans
Symbols 2", "DejaVu Sans", "Adobe Clean"). MS UI Gothic's stand-in is Adobe Clean (no star), so in a Neutron prefix the
star comes from the Segoe UI Symbol stand-in, the last link, where Windows takes MS UI Gothic's.
Not covered: Wine has no SystemLink entry for Segoe UI (Windows has one); it would change nothing here, since win32u looks
links up by the realized face (Adobe Clean), not the requested Segoe UI. GDI+ text (Wine's gdiplus does no font linking
and does not see Replacement families; Windows' GDI+ draws the star) and DirectWrite's system fallback (its 2600-26FF row
names "Noto Sans Symbols2", not the installed "Noto Sans Symbols 2"); Bridge's menus use neither.
Lab (runtime 11.10-185bf, Bridge 16.0.8, same win32u, same registry map, n=2 per arm): stars drawn 2/2 (B-F1, B-F2) and
2/2 more with the menu change on (M-*); boxes 2/2 with NEUTRON_FONTLINK_REPLACEMENT=0 (B-K1, B-K2). With the map written by
the starfont CLI through wine reg (C-cli1): stars, n=1. Path check: SystemLink entries pointing straight at DejaVu Sans
drew stars, a DirectWrite-only name did not (B-X, B-Y).
Kill switch NEUTRON_FONTLINK_REPLACEMENT=0.
--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -881,6 +881,13 @@
     return NULL;
 }
 
+static BOOL neutron_fontlink_replacement(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_FONTLINK_REPLACEMENT" ); on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static struct gdi_font_face *find_face_from_filename( const WCHAR *file_name, const WCHAR *family_name )
 {
     struct gdi_font_family *family;
@@ -896,7 +903,24 @@
     }
 
     if (!(family = find_family_from_name( family_name ))) return NULL;
-    return family_find_face_from_filename( family, file_name );
+    if ((face = family_find_face_from_filename( family, file_name ))) return face;
+    /* NEUTRON: a font link names Microsoft's file ("SEGUISYM.TTF,Segoe UI Symbol"). When that family
+       is only present as a Replacement (HKCU\Software\Wine\Fonts\Replacements), its stand-in's file
+       never has that name, so the link was dropped and a glyph Windows takes from the linked font
+       (U+2605 from Segoe UI Symbol) drew as a box. The Replacement says the stand-in IS that family:
+       link to its regular face. NEUTRON_FONTLINK_REPLACEMENT=0 restores file-only matching. */
+    if (family->replacement && neutron_fontlink_replacement())
+    {
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( face, get_family_face_list(family), struct gdi_font_face, entry )
+        {
+            if (!face->file || (face->ntmFlags & (NTM_ITALIC | NTM_BOLD))) continue;
+            face->refcount++;
+            TRACE( "link %s,%s -> replacement face %s\n", debugstr_w(file_name), debugstr_w(family_name),
+                   debugstr_w(face->full_name) );
+            return face;
+        }
+    }
+    return NULL;
 }
 
 static BOOL add_family_replacement( const WCHAR *new_name, const WCHAR *replace )
